==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|fiu-fin-pro|*pardas}}, borrowed from {{der|fi|gem-pro|*bardaz||edge}}, compare {{cog|non|barð||brim, verge}}. Cognates include {{cog|et|parras}}, {{cog|liv|pārdaz}}, {{cog|lud|pardaz}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-p}}

===Noun===
{{fi-noun}}

# [[brink]], [[verge]], [[edge]]
#: {{ux|fi|tuhon '''partaalla'''|on the brink of destruction}}
#: {{ux|fi|olla haudan '''partaalla'''|to have one foot in the grave}}
#:: to be [[on one's last legs]]
# {{n-g|In [[ulkopaikallissija#Finnish|external locative cases]], used to being close to something, usually figuratively}}; [[about]] (to)
#: {{ux|fi|Hän oli itkun '''partaalla'''.|She was about to cry.}}
# {{lb|fi|nautical}} [[rail]]

====Usage notes====
In the sense "brink, verge, edge" rarely used except in [[adessive]] (on), [[ablative]] (from) or [[allative]] (onto).

